  "text": "# Water under LDA\n\nMOLECULES holds water at its experimental geometry in the minimal STO-3G basis, solved twice. Restricted Hartree–Fock gives E = −74.963023 E_h. METHOD LDA gives E = −74.732041 E_h: Kohn–Sham with the local density approximation, Slater exchange plus VWN5 correlation.\n\nLDA's exchange–correlation energy is an integral over the density, so it is summed on a molecular grid: 67,950 points, a Becke partition of Treutler–Ahlrichs radial shells and 302-point Lebedev spheres. The grid's own error is printed, never hidden: it integrates the density to ∫ρ = 10.000001 for ten electrons. E_xc = −8.875980 E_h. The energy agrees with PySCF's RKS lda,vwn on the same grid to 3e-14 E_h.\n\n**The picture is VIEW Δ LDA−RHF**, where LDA puts more density: ρ_LDA − ρ_RHF, formed from D_LDA − D_RHF in double precision and drawn as a signed field. One colour is where LDA puts more density, the other where RHF does. Sampled at 48³ cell centres over the box, it runs from −0.0066 to +0.0100 a.u. Both densities hold the same ten electrons, so LDA moves charge and adds none.\n\nThe two solves are kept side by side: press RHF in METHOD and LDA again, and nothing is solved twice. Under LDA the real-time run, TDA, the drive, the register and VIBRATE stand down, because their operators are RHF's.\n"
 }
